{
    "map": {
        "class_codes.descr": "The class code values for the points representing the power lines.",
        "class_codes.title": "Power Line Class Codes",
        "description": "Extracts 3D line features modeling power lines \nfrom classified point cloud data.",
        "eliminate_wind.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies how wind correction will be applied to the output power lines. Wind correction will only be applied for catenary curves that span a distance longer than the value specified in the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Minimum Span for Wind Correction</span> parameter.</p><ul><li>Checked—The power lines will be adjusted to simulate the elimination of the impact of wind.</li><li>Unchecked—The power lines will be adjusted to achieve a better fit for the impact of wind. This is the default.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "eliminate_wind.title": "Eliminate wind",
        "end_point_search_radius.descr": "The distance that will be used to identify a common suspension point for power line segments connected to the same distribution pole or transmission tower. The default is 10 meters.",
        "end_point_search_radius.title": "End Point Search Radius",
        "in_point_cloud.descr": "The LAS dataset layer containing points classified as power lines.",
        "in_point_cloud.title": "Input Point Cloud",
        "line_tolerance.descr": "The distance that will be used to establish the accuracy of the output power line. A larger distance will result in the creation of less vertices per line, yielding a more coarse representation of the power line when compared with a smaller distance. The default is 1 centimeter.",
        "line_tolerance.title": "Output Line Tolerance",
        "max_sampling_gap.descr": "The largest gap that can exist in a given span of a power line. The catenary curve being modeled from a set of power line points will be extended by this distance to find other points that fit the same power line. The default is 5 meters.",
        "max_sampling_gap.title": "Maximum Wire Sampling Gap",
        "max_wind_deviation.descr": "The maximum angle that the wind is expected to deviate a given power line. The default is 10 degrees.",
        "max_wind_deviation.title": "Maximum Deviation Angle",
        "min_length.descr": "The shortest wire length that can be used to determine the presence of a common end point. The default is 5 meters.",
        "min_length.title": "Minimum Wire Length",
        "min_line_length.descr": "The minimum 3D length of the output wires. Lines that have a length shorter than the value specified for this parameter will be omitted from the output.",
        "min_line_length.title": "Minimum Power Line Length",
        "min_wind_span.descr": "The shortest distance a power line span can be to apply wind correction when generating the output power line. The default is 60 meters.",
        "min_wind_span.title": "Minimum Span for Wind Correction",
        "out_3d_lines.descr": "The 3D lines modeling the power lines.",
        "out_3d_lines.title": "Output 3D Lines",
        "params.category1": "Wind Correction",
        "params.category2": "End Point Adjustment",
        "point_tolerance.descr": "The distance used to establish the points that belong to a given power line. The default is 80 centimeters.",
        "point_tolerance.title": "Point Tolerance",
        "separation_distance.descr": "The distance apart points must be to determine if they belong to different power lines. The default is 1 meter.",
        "separation_distance.title": "Wire Separation Distance",
        "summary": "Extracts 3D line features modeling power lines from classified point cloud data.",
        "title": "Extract Power Lines From Point Cloud",
        "wind_correction.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies whether the output power lines will be adjusted for the influence of wind. When wind correction is applied, it can be used to either improve the fitting of wind modified points or model the resting state of the power lines when no wind is acting on them. The type of wind correction is specified using the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Eliminate wind</span> parameter.</p><ul><li>Checked—The power lines will be adjusted for the influence of the wind. This is the default.</li><li>Unchecked—An attempt will be made to fit the points without additional adjustments for the wind.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "wind_correction.title": "Adjust for wind distortion"
    }
}
